From 31cb63b26d224c3945163102751720fe79ec0587 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramiz Mehran <ramiz.mehran@meesho.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:30:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: add agy provider

Adds Google's Antigravity CLI (agy) as a fourth proxied provider.
AGY differs from claude/codex/gemini in three ways, each needing a
small extension to the provider contract:

- Plain-text stdout: agy --print emits no NDJSON. New optional
  ProviderConfig.emitsJson flag (default true); when false, the
  session manager skips the line-by-line JSON parser, accumulates raw
  stdout, and synthesizes text + result events on process exit.
- No session id on stdout: agy records conversation ids in
  ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/cache/last_conversations.json keyed by
  workspace path. New optional extractSessionIdFromExit(workspaceDir)
  hook reads it after each run so the next request can resume via
  --conversation <id>.
- No --model flag: model selection lives in
  ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json. The launcher persists the
  --model value there at proxy startup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
